--- verdict ---
PASS — the deliberate USB lease route (I-1) works end-to-end on the live board:
  S2  plain lease stays TCP (no USB dial anywhere)
  S3  `lease --usb`: 4.96s — RTS-pulse reboot, 4.5s drain (3781B ROM prefix),
      daemon log line + CLI stdout both carry the exact T10 warning
  S4  eval over the warm USB controller (return 42), status connected
  S5  release tears down both namespaces over USB
  S6  daemon stop closes the CDC port

OBSERVATION (board-side, fw repo scope — no daemon change): closing the USB
CDC port is INVISIBLE to the board (no FIN analogue; keepalive probes on a
detached CDC cannot fail), so the USB session's controller slot stays wedged
and later TCP hellos are forced observer past the 25s arbitration window
(S6b–S6d). Recovery = one headless CDC open (reboot, no hello — t10 phase-0
idiom), after which the daemon takes the TCP controller again: connected=yes,
wifi_state=up (S6d). Matches ErrControllerSlotHeld's guidance (USB reboot is
the last resort); flagged for the fw backlog.

